        "essence_text": "A harrowing, intensely realistic drama that turns a shocking crime into an examination of adolescence, family love, and the social forces shaping young masculinity. Its sustained visual momentum creates an unusually immediate experience, making conversations feel as suspenseful as confrontations. The performances are intimate and devastating, especially as parents and investigators struggle to understand what they failed to see. This is deeply thought-provoking television, built for focused viewing rather than comfort or casual background watching."
